    "knowledge_point": "Adding Rational Expressions in One Variable With Common Factors in the Denominators",
    "problem": "Given that $\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}=t$ and $\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v}=r,$ what is $t+r?$",
    "worked_solution": "We wish to add the following fractions:\n\n$$\nt+r=\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v}\n$$\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of $2(3+2v)$ if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{3-5v}{3+2v} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3-5v}{3+2v} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v}{2(3+2v)}+\\frac{2(3-5v)}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v+2(3-5v)}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{7v+6-10v}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{6-3v}{2(3+2v)} & = \\\\ \\frac{3(2-v)}{2(3+2v)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
